Yes. What you are describing is essentially a universal machine-health and diagnostic layer inside CoreGrid—but there is an important distinction:
A device does not necessarily have one universal “health code.” Different machines expose their internal state through different interfaces and protocols. A modern car is a particularly good example because its electronic control units (ECUs) continuously monitor sensors and components and can expose diagnostic trouble codes, live measurements, fault states, and other telemetry.
For CoreGrid, I would not build a giant database saying “error code X = broken component Y.” That would become a brittle catalog.
I would build a Universal Physical Diagnostics & Predictive Maintenance Engine.

