Knowledge must be temporally scoped.

Law 11

Source authority is contextual, not universal.

Law 12

Independent evidence matters more than duplicated sources.

Law 13

Sensitive knowledge remains governed by authorization.

Law 14

Summaries never replace underlying evidence.

Law 15

Inference must never silently become observation.

Law 16

Knowledge corrections must preserve lineage.

Law 17

Every important conclusion must be explainable through evidence and derivation.

Law 18

Knowledge quality is continuously evaluated.

Law 19

Knowledge gaps are first-class objects.

Law 20

CoreGrid must know the difference between what it knows, what it believes, what it predicts, and what it does not know.


